  85:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  *
  86:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  * Accesses memory in order
  87:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  * Note: this does not write the codewords as -1 or +1 as the green machine does
  88:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  * instead, just 0 and 1 is used.
  89:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  * The resulting hadamard transform has:
  90:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  * all values are halved
  91:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  * the first entry is 64 too high
  92:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  *
  93:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  * @param[out] dest Structure that contain the expanded codeword
  94:/home/reo/Documents/Repository/sca-2026/lib/crypto_kem/hqc128/pqclean/reed_muller.c ****  * @param[in] src Structure that contain the codeword
